Message-ID: <7.0.1.0.2.20060223092649.0241e6c0@stat.psu.edu>

It all depends on whether the dye-swaps are technical or biological reps.

If they are biological reps, there is only one blocking factor 
(array) which handles the duplicate spots on the same array.

If they are technical reps, there is a 2nd blocking factor (RNA 
source) which should be accounted for.

--Naomi

